{
  "dom_id": "step-t5310",
  "name": "Relaxing Variable Constraints",
  "problem": "So far, we have kept the domains of the plane polar coordinates restricted to $r\\geq 0$ and $\\theta\\in [0,2\\pi).$ What happens if we lift these restrictions?\n\nConsider the equation $r=\\theta$ with the domain restrictions $r\\geq 0$ and $\\theta\\in [0,2\\pi)$ which defines the surface shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14220175/assets/84737b12a1689fe2ac03ab09572e4c396d35493f55df5d65af80eeb8c5ae5676.png)\n\nSuppose we remove the restriction $\\theta\\in[0,2\\pi)$ so that it can be any number. What would the surface look like then?\n\nIf we remove the restriction on $\\theta,$ we obtain more spirals. For example, the diagram below shows $r=\\theta$ for $\\theta \\in [0, 4\\pi).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14220175/assets/568291daf47340265d97a121f0b7b927233f2698e87e0d5adebbba640ff20afe.png)\n\nWe can also lift the restriction $r \\geq 0$ so $r$ can take negative values. Typically, allowing negative values of $r$ adds $\\pi$ to the parameter $\\theta.$ So, we have\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/foundations/14220175/assets/ca3b8d2af7866d922a3b017a506790de4f3eca2dfb7e9385c87fbae0051a5ed3.svg)",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
  "html": "<div id=\"step-t5310\" class=\"step\" style=\"display: block;\">\n    \n               \n                <div class=\"tutorial\">\n                    <div class=\"stepHeader\">\n                        <div class=\"stepName\"><span class=\"stepType\">Relaxing Variable Constraints</span></div>       \n                        <div class=\"helpButton\" stepid=\"t5310\">?</div>\n                    </div>                    \n    \n                    <style type=\"text/css\">\n                            .mjpage .MJX-monospace {\n                            font-family: monospace\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage .MJX-sans-serif {\n                            font-family: sans-serif\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage {\n                            display: inline;\n                            font-style: normal;\n                            font-weight: normal;\n                            line-height: normal;\n                            font-size: 100%;\n                            font-size-adjust: none;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            text-align: left;\n                            text-transform: none;\n                            letter-spacing: normal;\n                            word-spacing: normal;\n                            word-wrap: normal;\n                            white-space: nowrap;\n                            float: none;\n                            direction: ltr;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage * {\n                            transition: none;\n                            -webkit-transition: none;\n                            -moz-transition: none;\n                            -ms-transition: none;\n                            -o-transition: none\n                            }\n\n                            .mjx-svg-href {\n                            fill: blue;\n                            stroke: blue\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox {\n                            display: table!important\n                            }\n\n                            .MathJax_SVG_LineBox span {\n                            display: table-cell!important;\n                            width: 10000em!important;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            padding: 0;\n                            border: 0;\n                            margin: 0\n                            }\n\n                            .mjpage__block {\n                            text-align: center;\n                            margin: 1em 0em;\n                            position: relative;\n                            display: block!important;\n                            text-indent: 0;\n                            max-width: none;\n                            max-height: none;\n                            min-width: 0;\n                            min-height: 0;\n                            width: 100%\n                            }</style><p>So far, we have kept the domains of the plane polar coordinates restricted to <span class=\"mjpage\"><svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"5.31ex\" height=\"2.343ex\" style=\"vertical-align: -0.505ex;\" viewBox=\"0 -791.3 2286.1 1008.6\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-labelledby=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">\n<title id=\"MathJax-SVG-1-Title\">r\\geq 0</title>\n<defs aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<path stroke-width=\"1\" id=\"E1-MJMATHI-72\" d=\"M21 287Q22 290 23 295T28 317T38 348T5